<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Świdnica</h1><p class="st-meta">1291 CE – 1392 CE · capital Świdnica</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Piast duchy below the Sudetes whose duke Bolko II was the last Silesian prince independent of Bohemia, until his lands passed to the Bohemian crown in 1392.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolko-i-the-strict">Bolko I the Strict</a>, already Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jawor">Jawor</a>, acquired <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swidnica">Świdnica</a> around 1291 and built a strong duchy along the Bohemian border. On his death in 1301 his son Bernard received Świdnica, which became a separate duchy. Bernard married a daughter of the Polish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wladyslaw-i-lokietek">Władysław I the Elbow-high</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swidnica">Świdnica</a> was a prosperous town of cloth, beer and trade on the routes to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Bohemia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolko-ii-the-small">Bolko II the Small</a>, Bernard's son, refused to accept Bohemian overlordship, ruling as an independent prince and uniting Świdnica with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jawor">Jawor</a> in 1346. Without sons, he arranged the marriage of his niece Anne to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iv">Charles IV</a>, making the Bohemian crown his heir.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolko-ii-the-small">Bolko II</a> died in 1368, his widow Agnes ruled until her death in 1392, when the duchy passed to the Bohemian crown. It later went to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, and has been Polish since 1945; its Peace Church is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">World Heritage Site</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-swidnica.jpg" alt="Duchy of Świdnica" width="320" height="241"><figcaption>Image: Kateryna Baiduzha · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https:/